  "patch_commits": [
    {
      "sha": "3b9d5178999411b9181884a7612b271172c4fde4",
      "parents": [
        "1fe3e0a29bef2fa314944f958d9e21119e14e95b"
      ],
      "message": "Rint join (RIMPR-01/02): consume the whole last frame and check float64/int64 at the entrance, tests first (join test 78/135 on the unfixed module -> 138/138)\n\nRIMPR-01: every non-empty row of a row section is counted and a column-count mismatch rejects (row_width); each consumed required column must appear exactly once (header_duplicate); TIMESTEP and NUMBER OF sections must be exactly one integer token over their whole body (int_token); every line of the last frame must belong to one of the four known sections once (frame_layout: unknown ITEM section, repeated section, non-empty line before the first frame, trailing tokens on the TIMESTEP/NUMBER OF header line); exactly three box bound lines. All reject before any gate runs, so the plan inherits join_gate_failed.\nRIMPR-02: finiteness is judged on the float64 values actually used (a fixed-point or 1e309 token that Decimal calls finite but float64 makes +/-inf rejects as nonfinite_value), the scaffold micrometre conversion must stay finite, and integer tokens outside int64 reject as int_token instead of raising OverflowError.\nNormal inputs unchanged: real_14 457/457 particles and 660 AM-AM areas, case15 104/104 and 119, D19 declared reuse through plan and quantitative gate, duplicate normal-width rows still reject with the same codes. Blank-line handling kept identical to the old reader (three pinning checks). JOIN_VERSION -> g_geo_g_frame_v3. step3_sigma.py and the 32 sealed files untouched. Census 8/8, order 6/6, discipline checker 0 errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019HKnbzGsY9U5Gyw4qGqqzA",
      "files": [
        "scripts/rint_iface_join.py",
        "scripts/test_rint_g2_join.py"
      ],
      "sealed_touched": []
    },
    {
      "sha": "2b9efa253edbf455c2e1abfef1d60e51818e01f8",
      "parents": [
        "3ad8fd351baade4361fd0f141209411832459935"
      ],
      "message": "Rint G2 general gate (Codex 10-15 recheck Q7, first author approved 10-20): membrane values r_face must be finite and non-negative before assembly, tests first; update the short Codex recheck request (same-class hardening ratified, Q7 implemented in this commit) and the progress records\n\niface_require_quantitative checked the row fingerprint but not the membrane values, and the assembly only\napplies a film where r_face > 0, so a plan whose fingerprint was recomputed after setting one film row to\nNaN or a negative value silently dropped the film, and +inf zeroed the face.  The gate now requires every\naxis row's r_face to be finite and >= 0 right after the fingerprint check (r = 0 and cut tombstones allowed),\nso solve_sigma_z refuses before assembly.  The gate only runs when an iface plan is passed; the iface-off\npath is unchanged.  step3_sigma.py is outside the sealed 32 files.\n\n- test_rint_g2_am_iface.py new case Q7 (4 checks): NaN / -r_face / +inf film row with recomputed fingerprint\n  = gate ValueError naming r_face and no CG call; positive controls RRM r = 0 plan, normal RRM plan (Codex\n  values, rel 1e-9), CNC r = 0 plan bit-identical to OFF, finite positive mutation passes and solves.\n  Unfixed code 133/136 (the three must-raise checks), fixed 136/136.\n- test_rint_g2_rrm.py N9b split: the cut-deletion bypass (finite values, still outside the general gate)\n  keeps its recorded sigma; the film-NaN plan must now be refused by the general solver, with the blocked\n  bypass size recorded through the registered r = 0 plan (same assembled matrix).  Unfixed 54/55, fixed 55/55.\n- Unfixed counts re-verified by unpacking the tests-only state into a new empty folder.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019HKnbzGsY9U5Gyw4qGqqzA",
